From: Thomas Karpiniec <tom.karpiniec@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: propagate platform mac_finish errors

The platform mac_finish callback can fail when reconfiguring the MAC-side
interface. In particular, Qualcomm ETHQOS returns a SerDes calibration
timeout when switching between SGMII and 2500BASE-X on the IQ-8275.

Return the callback's error to phylink instead of reporting success.
Phylink already logs mac_finish failures and suppresses carrier until a
subsequent configuration succeeds. Retain success when no callback exists.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not submitted]
Signed-off-by: Thomas Karpiniec <tom.karpiniec@outlook.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -1048,8 +1048,8 @@ static int stmmac_mac_finish(struct phylink_config *config, unsigned int mode,
 	struct stmmac_priv *priv = netdev_priv(ndev);
 
 	if (priv->plat->mac_finish)
-		priv->plat->mac_finish(ndev, priv->plat->bsp_priv, mode,
-				       interface);
+		return priv->plat->mac_finish(ndev, priv->plat->bsp_priv, mode,
+					     interface);
 
 	return 0;
 }
